{
    "guided.category.movement_terrain": "Movement, terrain, and crossings",
    "guided.movement.complete": "Lesson complete. Replay it or return to the guided browser.",

    "guided.movement.capture.title": "Read lines, blockers, and captures",
    "guided.movement.capture.explanation": "Sliding pieces stop at the first piece on a line. A friendly piece blocks the line; an enemy on the first reachable square can be captured.",
    "guided.movement.capture.hint.1": "The South Rook has one blocked file but an open rank toward the enemy Pawn.",
    "guided.movement.capture.hint.2": "Move the Rook from (1, 6) to the enemy Pawn on (4, 6).",

    "guided.movement.knight_jump.title": "Jump with the Knight",
    "guided.movement.knight_jump.explanation": "Knights use their L-shaped move and ignore intervening pieces, mountains, and edges; only their landing square must be legal.",
    "guided.movement.knight_jump.hint.1": "Look beyond the mountain markers for an L-shaped landing square.",
    "guided.movement.knight_jump.hint.2": "Move the Knight from (2, 6) to (3, 4).",

    "guided.movement.forest.title": "Enter a forest deliberately",
    "guided.movement.forest.explanation": "A sliding piece may enter a forest, but its ray stops on that forest square. Forests use both tint and a tree marker.",
    "guided.movement.forest.hint.1": "The Rook can approach the marked forest along its open file.",
    "guided.movement.forest.hint.2": "Move the Rook from (1, 6) onto the forest at (1, 3).",

    "guided.movement.mountain.title": "Jump a mountain blocker",
    "guided.movement.mountain.explanation": "Mountains are impassable landing squares and block sliding rays. Knights may still jump over them to a clear destination.",
    "guided.movement.mountain.hint.1": "Use the piece whose movement does not trace the intervening squares.",
    "guided.movement.mountain.hint.2": "Move the Knight from (1, 6) to (2, 4).",

    "guided.movement.bridge.title": "Cross where the river opens",
    "guided.movement.bridge.explanation": "River edges block movement. Bridge and ford symbols mark traversable edges without changing the movement shape of the piece.",
    "guided.movement.bridge.hint.1": "Find the bridge marker in the otherwise continuous river boundary.",
    "guided.movement.bridge.hint.2": "Cross the bridge with the Rook on file 3.",

    "guided.movement.tower_rook.title": "Use gates and a linked tower Rook",
    "guided.movement.tower_rook.explanation": "Gates are open crossings. Walls block pieces, except a friendly Rook standing on the tower linked to that exact projected wall.",
    "guided.movement.tower_rook.hint.1": "The tower emblem identifies the Rook that can project through its linked wall.",
    "guided.movement.tower_rook.hint.2": "Move the tower Rook from (3, 5) through the wall toward (3, 3).",

    "guided.movement.assessment_cross.title": "Assessment: establish contact",
    "guided.movement.assessment_cross.explanation": "Apply the crossing rules without a move hint. Put the Rook across the river while keeping the South King safe.",
    "guided.movement.assessment_capture.title": "Assessment: make a safe capture",
    "guided.movement.assessment_capture.explanation": "The Apprentice may change the position. Find a legal continuation that captures the marked enemy Pawn; no exact move is prescribed.",

    "guided.category.realm": "Settlements, governance, and production",
    "guided.realm.complete": "Realm lesson complete. Replay it or continue from the guided browser.",
    "guided.realm.claim.title": "Claim a settlement and preserve its founder",
    "guided.realm.claim.explanation": "A Pawn landing on a neutral settlement claims it. That exact Pawn becomes the founder, whose identity remains part of the settlement state.",
    "guided.realm.claim.hint.1": "Only a Pawn can claim the neutral settlement in this position.",
    "guided.realm.claim.hint.2": "Move the South Pawn from (3, 5) onto the settlement at (3, 4).",
    "guided.realm.governance.title": "Complete a continuous governed cycle",
    "guided.realm.governance.explanation": "Ownership alone is not governance. A friendly Rook, Bishop, or Queen needs an unobstructed line to the founder; progress advances only when continuity survives the full owner cycle.",
    "guided.realm.governance.hint.1": "The South Rook currently has a clear line to the founder. End North's turn without interrupting it.",
    "guided.realm.governance.hint.2": "Use Hold for North and observe the development event at South's owner boundary.",
    "guided.realm.production.title": "Place a produced Pawn",
    "guided.realm.production.explanation": "An established, continuously governed settlement accumulates production. Readiness creates a mandatory placement choice using only the highlighted legal squares.",
    "guided.realm.production.hint.1": "Choose any highlighted empty square adjacent to the settlement; the choice does not consume another command turn.",
    "guided.realm.production.hint.2": "Press Enter on a highlighted square such as (2, 2), or click it.",
    "guided.realm.transfer.title": "Observe a contested transfer",
    "guided.realm.transfer.explanation": "The hostile Pawn already contests this settlement. If it survives until its owner's next boundary, ownership and founder identity transfer while established progress persists.",
    "guided.realm.transfer.hint.1": "North can allow the pending transfer by ending this turn without removing the candidate.",
    "guided.realm.transfer.hint.2": "Use Hold for North and inspect the typed transfer event.",
    "guided.realm.transfer_cancel.title": "Cancel a hostile transfer",
    "guided.realm.transfer_cancel.explanation": "A transfer candidate is not yet the owner. Capturing it or forcing it off the settlement cancels the pending transfer and preserves the current owner.",
    "guided.realm.transfer_cancel.hint.1": "North has a Rook on the same open file as the contesting Pawn.",
    "guided.realm.transfer_cancel.hint.2": "Capture the Pawn on (3, 3) with the North Rook.",
    "guided.realm.practice_claim.title": "Assessment: extend the realm",
    "guided.realm.practice_claim.explanation": "Claim the neutral settlement while preserving the two existing founder lines. The Steward will answer using normal realm-aware evaluation.",
    "guided.realm.practice_govern.title": "Assessment: retain shared governance",
    "guided.realm.practice_govern.explanation": "After the reply, keep both established settlements governed and the new settlement owned. More than one defensible continuation is acceptable.",

    "guided.category.royal": "Promotion, royal safety, and combined play",
    "guided.royal.complete": "Royal lesson complete. Replay it or continue from the guided browser.",
    "guided.royal.en_passant.title": "Use the one-turn en passant window",
    "guided.royal.en_passant.explanation": "North has just used its unmoved Pawn's two-square advance. South may capture it as though it moved one square, but only on this immediate reply.",
    "guided.royal.en_passant.hint.1": "The South Pawn beside the advanced Pawn has a diagonal capture onto the square it crossed.",
    "guided.royal.en_passant.hint.2": "Move the South Pawn from (4, 3) to (3, 2).",
    "guided.royal.promotion_knight.title": "Recruit the only unlocked piece",
    "guided.royal.promotion_knight.explanation": "Promotion is a mandatory choice. Control scores owned settlements once, governed settlements once, and established settlements twice. With score 0 only Knight is unlocked; Bishop, Rook, and Queen require 2, 4, and 8.",
    "guided.royal.promotion_knight.hint.1": "The locked choices show the current-control thresholds; waiting alone never unlocks them.",
    "guided.royal.promotion_knight.hint.2": "Choose Knight, the only legal recruitment in this position.",
    "guided.royal.promotion_bishop.title": "Choose for the position, not maximum value",
    "guided.royal.promotion_bishop.explanation": "Two established and governed settlements produce control 8, unlocking every kind. This batch freezes that eligibility for both Pawns. Recruit the Bishop requested by the position, not the automatic Queen.",
    "guided.royal.promotion_bishop.hint.1": "All four choices are legal; only Bishop meets this lesson's positional objective.",
    "guided.royal.promotion_bishop.hint.2": "Promote the west Pawn to Bishop.",
    "guided.royal.promotion_rook.title": "Resolve the frozen batch",
    "guided.royal.promotion_rook.explanation": "The second mandatory choice retains the same start-of-batch score even if the first choice changes the board. Later batches recompute current control and can relock pieces after lost territory.",
    "guided.royal.promotion_rook.hint.1": "The remaining Pawn still offers the batch's frozen choices.",
    "guided.royal.promotion_rook.hint.2": "Promote the east Pawn to Rook rather than Queen.",
    "guided.royal.answer_check.title": "Answer check before realm progress",
    "guided.royal.answer_check.explanation": "Check suspends every plan: Hold is illegal and a pinned or irrelevant realm move cannot expose the King. Block this file with the Bishop. The checking move has stolen the realm tempo you might otherwise spend on settlement continuity.",
    "guided.royal.answer_check.hint.1": "Several royal evasions may be legal, but this objective asks for the safe blocking move that preserves material.",
    "guided.royal.answer_check.hint.2": "The Knight on (3, 6) is pinned to the King. Move the Bishop from (5, 6) to (4, 5).",
    "guided.royal.castle.title": "Castle only through safe authored squares",
    "guided.royal.castle.explanation": "Castling is available only on a scenario-authored route while King and Rook rights remain, intervening squares are clear, and the King is not in, through, or into check. One King move relocates both pieces.",
    "guided.royal.castle.hint.1": "Select the South King; the castling destination is two files east.",
    "guided.royal.castle.hint.2": "Move the King from (4, 7) to (6, 7).",
    "guided.royal.checkmate.title": "Finish a canonical checkmate",
    "guided.royal.checkmate.explanation": "Checkmate is check with no legal evasion. Find a protected Queen move that attacks the North King and covers every escape; the normal outcome detector ends the match.",
    "guided.royal.checkmate.hint.1": "The South King protects the square immediately diagonal to it.",
    "guided.royal.checkmate.hint.2": "Move the Queen from (1, 2) to (1, 1).",
    "guided.royal.draw.title": "Resolve a draw offer",
    "guided.royal.draw.explanation": "North has offered a draw. Accepting is a canonical mandatory response and ends the match without a winner; repetition can also produce a draw through normal outcome rules.",
    "guided.royal.draw.hint.1": "Use the draw-response control to accept North's offer.",
    "guided.royal.practice_finish.title": "Assessment: balance crown and realm",
    "guided.royal.practice_finish.explanation": "Play this bounded small map against the Steward under normal victory rules. Manage checks, settlements, and promotion timing; no move is prescribed, and any canonical match outcome completes the assessment.",
    "guided.royal.practice_finish.hint.1": "Before each realm move, verify whether either King is threatened and whether your founder lines remain governed.",
    "guided.royal.practice_finish.hint.2": "Promotion access follows current control, so defend useful settlements before racing a Pawn to court.",
}
